Icon set "usaicon"
------------------

Introduction:
  This package is a mark icon set for hns (HyperNikkiSystem).
  For about hns, please see http://www.h14m.org/.

Icon list:
  Icons which are included in this package are listed below, order of
  argument to MARK command, file name.
  All icons are saved in PNG format.

  (^^)     usaniko.png
  (-_-)    usamesen.png
  (^^;     usaase.png
  (;_;)    usauru.png
  (T_T)    usauru2.png
  v(^^)    usav.png
  m(__)m   usapeko.png
  !!       usadoki.png
  ??       usahatena.png
  !?       usanaze.png
  (laugh)  usasho.png
  :-)      usasmile.png, usasmile2.png
  :-(      usaheno.png, usaheno2.png
  :-P      usabe.png, usabe2.png
  /(._.)   usamemo.png
  back     usaback.png
  fool     usabaka.png

Usage:
  I show an example which built marks into theme.ph in the following.
  This is a case having put icons in ~/public_html/diary/usaicon/.

# Mark
package HNS::Hnf::Command::MARK;
# image size is automatically set
$List{"(^^)"} =  "usaicon/usaniko.png";
$List{"(-_-)"} =  "usaicon/usamesen.png";
$List{"(^^;"} = "usaicon/usaase.png";
$List{"(;_;)"} = "usaicon/usauru.png";
$List{"(T_T)"} = "usaicon/usauru2.png";
$List{"v(^^)"} = "usaicon/usav.png";
$List{"m(__)m"} = "usaicon/usapeko.png";
$List{"!!"} = "usaicon/usadoki.png";
$List{"??"} = "usaicon/usahatena.png";
$List{"!?"} = "usaicon/usanaze.png";
$List{"(laugh)"} = "usaicon/usasho.png";
$List{":-)"} = "usaicon/usasmile2.png";
$List{":-("} = "usaicon/usaheno2.png";
$List{":-P"} = "usaicon/usabe2.png";
$List{"/(._.)"} = "usaicon/usamemo.png";
$List{"back"} = "usaicon/usaback.png";
$List{"fool"} = "usaicon/usabaka.png";


